# V - Ugur interatomic potential, CANDIDATE, force-matched, switched
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * V_force_taper.ugur V
#
# Truncation: switched from 0.85 of each cutoff to the cutoff, quintic, C2 - energy is conserved in MD: measured drift within noise for copper (0.002 meV/atom/ns against 176 for its hard twin).  USE for molecular dynamics, which no hard set can do.  It pays for that on the dispersion: the switched sets average 12.6 % against the hard sets' 9.7 %, because switching the pair term off over the outer 15 % moves the force constants at the largest separations, which is the short-wavelength end, and nothing in the fit sees it
# MD: not screened.
#
# LATTICE STABILITY: this set is NOT a harmonic minimum.
# Along the Setyawan-Curtarolo path its frequencies reach -158.694 cm^-1,
# with 17.64 % of the sampled modes imaginary.  That is a separate
# failure from the 600 K screen above and is not covered by it.
#
# Nudge test: not run.
#
# Fitted to: DFT FORCES on displaced supercells of V, from the
# database cited here, with the cohesive energy, lattice constant and
# elastic constants kept as anchors.
# Source: Byggmastar, Nordlund, Djurabekova, Phys. Rev. Materials 4, 093802 (2020).
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
